<title>BELGIUM: Cockerill CMI unit gets export aid.</title>
<headline>Cockerill CMI unit gets export aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said on Friday it would grant export credits to  Cockerill Mechanical Industries, a unit of steel group Cockerill Sambre, for a contract to build a gas-fired power station in Turkey.</p>
<p>The power station is being built at Marmara Ereglesi by a consortium led by German engineering company  ABB Kraftwerke AG, a unit of the ABB group.</p>
<p>&quot;This project will bring the Belgian economy 500,000 man hours of work,&quot; the government said in a statement issued at the end of its weekly cabinet meeting. Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
